From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:17:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820-beyond2lte: Route Bluetooth
 SCO over the UART

The BCM4375 routes SCO audio to its PCM pins after reset.  On this board
those pins go to the SoC audio subsystem, which has no driver, so a
headset call has no path to the host.

Route SCO over the HCI transport instead, so that the Bluetooth stack
carries call audio itself.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
index a97def1a6f5..9be8afa51c0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
@@ -567,6 +567,14 @@ bluetooth {
 		device-wakeup-gpios = <&gpg2 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		interrupts-extended = <&gpa2 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		interrupt-names = "host-wakeup";
+		/*
+		 * The chip comes up routing SCO to its PCM pins, which on this
+		 * board go to the audio subsystem, not to anything the host can
+		 * read.  Route it over the UART instead, so that headset calls
+		 * work without the audio subsystem.  Read back from the chip:
+		 * 00 02 00 01 01 before, 01 02 00 01 01 after.
+		 */
+		brcm,bt-pcm-int-params = [01 02 00 01 01];
 	};
 };
 
